{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784202256,"nonce":"H3fSNvbnGn4WeBnyo+3Gr2OidMY=","title":"Wire the content-addressed workspace into the k8s execution path (ADR-0029, ADR-0007, ADR-0045). Today `Cas::materialize`/`ingest` exist in `scarab-storage-s3` but are never called on k8s, `build_pod` mounts no workspace, and `Executor::output` returns `None` — so no files flow between steps on a real cluster.","message":"Add to `build_pod` (`crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs`): an init-container that materializes the merged workspace of the step's `needs` into `/workspace` from the CAS, and a post-step ingest that snapshots `/workspace` back into the CAS and returns the root tree hash as `Executor::output`. Include `.git` in the snapshot (ADR-0045 §Workspace contents).\n\nThis is the keystone wiring: it simultaneously unblocks inter-step workspace passing, `outputs:`/`inputs:` enforcement (ADR-0035/0007), skip-if-unchanged on real clusters (ADR-0027), and is the mechanism the `clone` step's output flows through.\n\n\n- [ ] `build_pod` mounts `/workspace` and adds a CAS-materialize init-container fed by the step's `needs`\n- [ ] Post-step ingest snapshots `/workspace` (including `.git`) into the CAS; `Executor::output` returns the root hash\n- [ ] A 2-step pipeline where step A writes a file and step B (`needs: [A]`) reads it works on live Colima\n- [ ] Materialize pulls only files the node lacks (per-file merkle, ADR-0029)\n- [ ] Restart of a step re-materializes deterministically from the same CAS root\n\n\nNone - can start immediately","files":null}]}